Logic :

Solution -1 

Initialise map for storing frequency of each number
while size of map exceeds 2 , then move left pointer , and reduce its frequency in map
and , if the number in the map equals zero , which tells that the number if not in the window , hence remove that key
and , increment left pointer
add the element in map if it not present , otherwise , increase its frequency
if the size of map less than or equal to 2 , then calculate the window length

Solution - 2

Initialise map for storing frequency of each number
if size of map exceeds 2 , then move left pointer , and reduce its frequency in map
and , if the number in the map equals zero , which tells that the number if not in the window , hence remove that key
and , increment left pointer
add the element in map if it not present , otherwise , increase its frequency
if the size of map less than or equal to 2 , then calculate the window length


Intuition :
only difference of both solution is if condition and while loop


Code :

Solution -1  (Time complexity : O(2n) ~ O(n))

class Solution {
    public int totalFruit(int[] fruits) {
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
        int left=0;
        int maxlen=0;
        for(int right=0;right<fruits.length;right++){
            while(map.size()>2){
                map.put(fruits[left],map.get(fruits[left])-1);
                 if(map.getOrDefault(fruits[left],-1)==0){
                    map.remove(fruits[left]);
            }
            left++;
            }
           
            map.put(fruits[right],map.getOrDefault(fruits[right],0)+1);
            if(map.size()<=2){
                maxlen=Math.max(maxlen,right-left+1);
            }
        }
        return maxlen;
    }
}

